From ee6a4cb236e11178e597c4fc7c4f102b129af6d7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vinny Menichetti <vinny@collision.academy>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 14:11:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Review one estimate on its own terms instead of failing it as
 a comparison
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A case with a single estimate on file hit the two-estimate delta release
gate (R24/R26) and shipped nothing: "a run that read neither totals block
cannot ship". There was no comparison to gate. This adds the single-estimate
Forensic Estimate Review and routes the Reports card by estimate count.

- src/lib/reports/forensicSingle/: engine (reconcile to printed totals →
  deterministic rule catalog → verdict/exposure/checklist), report-plan
  routing (1 estimate → FORENSIC_SINGLE, 2 → FORENSIC_DELTA + CITATION_DENSITY),
  adapter from the platform's own readers (measured word lane via
  deltaEngine/rowCluster, text lane via estimatePlatform) and a pdf-lib
  renderer on the shared forensic Writer.
- POST /api/reports/forensic-estimate: resolves the case's estimate, prefers
  the measured word layer, answers 409 with the plan mode when the case
  carries a pair so the client continues with the two-estimate flow.
- Reports card renamed "Forensic Report w/ Citation Density Report"; in
  single mode the description, download label and email kind follow the
  plan and the Citation Density target selector is hidden.
- /api/reports/send accepts forensic_estimate_review.
- Writer.wrap folds text to WinAnsi before measuring width: a "→" in a
  finding sentence threw inside widthOfTextAtSize before any page drew.
- Tests: forensicSingle.test.ts (fixture parity with the hand-built review —
  12 findings, $0.00 unexplained, +$261.80 to +$290.60; real CCC print closes
  to $0.00 through the measured lane; routing; universality).

